WEBVTT

00:02.900 --> 00:04.740
A long, long time ago.

00:04.960 --> 00:07.640
A story from about a hundred years ago.

00:08.530 --> 00:13.280
Nadja, guided by
destiny, arrived in France.

00:17.480 --> 00:18.780
- NAAJA
- Nadja,

00:18.900 --> 00:20.170
With your eyes

00:20.171 --> 00:21.440
Kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:21.440 --> 00:22.650
- Nadja,
- NAAJA

00:22.690 --> 00:23.820
What do you see?

00:23.821 --> 00:24.950
Nani ga mieru

00:24.980 --> 00:26.425
Haruka tooku hikaru

00:26.426 --> 00:27.870
Shining in the far distance,

00:27.880 --> 00:29.070
The door to the future,

00:29.071 --> 00:30.260
Mirai no tobira

00:31.140 --> 00:32.880
That's what I'm searching for

00:32.881 --> 00:34.620
Sagashite iru

00:34.620 --> 00:38.230
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:42.540 --> 00:44.300
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:44.301 --> 00:46.060
Minna egao de aetara

00:46.140 --> 00:49.390
- I'm sure there would be no more fighting
- Arasoi mo kitto nakunaru

00:49.420 --> 00:51.025
It could be so much more fun

00:51.026 --> 00:52.630
Konna ni mo tanoshi kunaru

00:52.690 --> 00:54.400
The world is wide, but it's still one

00:54.401 --> 00:56.110
Sekai wa hiroi kedo hitotsu ne

00:56.470 --> 00:58.120
I can't see the end of the journey

00:58.121 --> 00:59.770
Tabi no owari wa mienai

00:59.890 --> 01:03.220
- God is the only one who could
possibly know - Kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:03.410 --> 01:07.000
- To the people who, someday, I will meet
again - Itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:07.040 --> 01:08.100
I will go waving

01:08.101 --> 01:09.160
Te wo furinagara

01:09.240 --> 01:12.570
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:12.571 --> 01:15.900
Toki ni wa BURUU ni naru hi mo aru kedo

01:15.970 --> 01:17.325
But I won't look back

01:17.326 --> 01:18.680
Ushiro mukanai

01:19.010 --> 01:21.490
Until the day my dream comes true

01:21.491 --> 01:23.970
Yume ga kanau hi made

01:24.260 --> 01:25.970
Nadja, Your smile

01:25.971 --> 01:27.680
NAAJA kimi no hohoemi wa

01:27.740 --> 01:29.410
Nadja, gives me courage

01:29.411 --> 01:31.080
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:31.150 --> 01:32.610
Under the blue sky,

01:32.611 --> 01:34.070
Aoi sora no shita de

01:34.170 --> 01:35.585
I will find the place

01:35.586 --> 01:37.000
Ashita no yukue

01:37.330 --> 01:39.285
where my future lies

01:39.286 --> 01:41.240
Mitsukeru kara

01:51.990 --> 01:54.280
Nadja and the troupe left Paris...

01:54.490 --> 01:57.740
and arrived in the
province of Lorraine in France.

02:02.230 --> 02:03.770
Sorry to be a bother...

02:05.560 --> 02:07.650
We're going to be here for a while.

02:07.770 --> 02:09.520
Don't even mention it!

02:09.520 --> 02:13.280
It's just a pasture in the countryside.
Stay as long as you want.

02:13.490 --> 02:15.780
Right?

02:16.320 --> 02:19.200
It's been a long time, now we can relax...

02:19.530 --> 02:21.790
Relax? What about the show?

02:21.790 --> 02:23.580
What's going to happen with the show?

02:23.580 --> 02:26.080
Oh, that... We won't be able
to do them for a while.

02:26.080 --> 02:28.420
You mean, we're taking a holiday?

02:29.500 --> 02:31.550
Well, yes, in a way..

02:32.170 --> 02:34.210
If you don't count that person...

02:34.260 --> 02:35.880
Huh? What person?

02:36.130 --> 02:37.510
A search for treasure?

02:37.720 --> 02:39.680
What's with those
primitive choice of words?

02:39.890 --> 02:41.510
Call it 'Treasure Hunting'!

02:41.760 --> 02:43.720
That 'Treasure Hunting'...

02:43.720 --> 02:45.480
and the troupe's holiday...

02:45.480 --> 02:47.310
What's the connection?

02:47.560 --> 02:50.190
Treasure hunting... it's every man's dream!

02:50.610 --> 02:53.070
Treasure hunting...
it's a man's reason for living!

02:53.530 --> 02:57.200
Treasure hunting... it's my life's work!

02:57.360 --> 02:59.570
But Master's job is being
the Troupe Master, right?

02:59.570 --> 03:04.910
Non, non, non! You don't... really...
understand my situation!

03:05.330 --> 03:08.080
My real identity' is...
the Treasure Hunter!

03:08.080 --> 03:10.920
In fact... a Troupe Master only
in between Treasure Hunts...

03:11.040 --> 03:13.130
that's how you can think of me.

03:13.380 --> 03:16.760
The reason I travel the world like this...

03:16.760 --> 03:18.970
is so that I can search for treasure!

03:19.140 --> 03:20.930
Oh, so that's why.

03:21.550 --> 03:22.930
I didn't know that...

03:23.100 --> 03:24.510
Now, I will reveal to you...

03:24.560 --> 03:27.680
my many exciting adventures!

03:30.770 --> 03:34.820
Once I hunted the treasure of a pirate
ship that plied the mighty oceans.

03:36.110 --> 03:37.440
On another occasion,

03:37.450 --> 03:40.450
I explored ancient ruins
in the depths of a jungle!

03:42.200 --> 03:43.780
And yet on another occasion..

03:43.780 --> 03:46.220
Pfft! You're tied up in all of them!

03:43.780 --> 03:44.830
a cave...

03:46.370 --> 03:50.120
But, are there really so many treasures
conveniently placed everywhere?

03:50.120 --> 03:53.750
Non, non, non! You don't
understand anything...!

03:54.090 --> 03:55.090
Look at this!

03:56.420 --> 03:57.460
Ah! This is...

03:57.720 --> 04:00.470
the treasure map we
received at the British Museum!

04:00.510 --> 04:01.380
That is correct.

04:01.510 --> 04:02.720
And read right here!

04:02.970 --> 04:04.240
Domremy...

04:04.580 --> 04:05.240
You mean...!

04:05.430 --> 04:07.270
There's a treasure in this village!?

04:07.560 --> 04:08.560
That is correct.

04:10.730 --> 04:11.850
Treasure...

04:12.190 --> 04:14.020
If I find the treasure...

04:14.230 --> 04:17.190
I might be able to build my own
personal mechanical automobile.

04:18.280 --> 04:21.200
After all, a man with a
car is in a different class.

04:21.570 --> 04:24.990
And, it makes it easier
to ask girls out on dates...

04:25.580 --> 04:27.910
Kennosuke! You're wonderful!

04:31.170 --> 04:32.210
Treasure...

04:32.750 --> 04:34.790
If I find the treasure...

04:34.920 --> 04:38.420
Maybe I can repair the fire damage
at the Applefield Orphanage...

04:38.710 --> 04:40.880
After all, it's still summer
so it's not a problem...

04:41.090 --> 04:44.340
But, it'll be bad for them if they
don't have a roof by winter...

04:44.680 --> 04:48.140
Nadja, thank you! Thank you!

04:49.270 --> 04:50.270
What do you think?

04:50.310 --> 04:52.850
Treasure hunting is the greatest, right?

04:53.480 --> 04:54.270
Yes...

04:54.480 --> 04:55.480
The greatest...

04:55.610 --> 04:57.940
That is the greatest!

05:07.890 --> 05:12.850
Treasure Hunting is Romantic!?

05:20.970 --> 05:22.470
It's so peaceful...

05:24.890 --> 05:27.300
Master! What kind of treasure is it?

05:27.390 --> 05:29.970
Please hurry up and tell us, Master!

05:30.020 --> 05:31.980
The treasure hidden in this village...

05:31.980 --> 05:32.980
it is...

05:33.060 --> 05:34.140
It is?

05:34.600 --> 05:36.230
The treasure of Jeanne d'Arc!

05:36.480 --> 05:37.730
Jeanne d'Arc...

05:38.980 --> 05:41.030
And... who is she?

05:41.650 --> 05:42.690
Jeanne d'Arc...

05:43.150 --> 05:44.490
The Maid from Lorraine...

05:44.950 --> 05:48.030
At the time of the Hundred Years War
with England five hundred years ago...

05:48.160 --> 05:49.740
She heard a message from God...

05:49.870 --> 05:53.870
and, by herself, she led the
losing French side to victory...

05:53.870 --> 05:55.210
Pretty great, eh?

05:55.210 --> 05:57.920
Yeah... Just like a Sengoku-era warrior.

05:58.290 --> 06:01.050
And, she also happens
to be from this village.

06:01.130 --> 06:02.130
What do you think?

06:02.260 --> 06:04.630
So... what's the treasure?

06:04.630 --> 06:07.010
Gold and jewels confiscated
from the English army.

06:07.140 --> 06:10.580
Or could it be buried treasure that she dug
from the earth according to God's messages

06:11.390 --> 06:13.100
B-Buried treasure?

06:13.350 --> 06:14.020
Well...

06:14.190 --> 06:16.770
If we go to the spot marked
on the map, we'll find out.

06:23.530 --> 06:24.530
Okay! We're here

06:24.530 --> 06:25.490
What! Already?

06:25.490 --> 06:26.280
That was quick!

06:26.410 --> 06:29.740
Yeah! Yeah! We found the treasure!

06:29.740 --> 06:30.620
Huh?

06:30.660 --> 06:31.830
H-Huh?

06:32.290 --> 06:33.700
Are we in the right place?

06:33.700 --> 06:35.460
Y-Yeah... there's no mistake...

06:35.960 --> 06:38.080
But... this is...

06:38.630 --> 06:40.290
A... vegetable... stand...

06:42.050 --> 06:44.130
A... vegetable... stand...

06:44.340 --> 06:45.590
That is correct.

06:45.590 --> 06:48.130
Jeanne d'Arc is the pride of the villagers.

06:48.140 --> 06:50.090
Not only in this village, but...

06:50.100 --> 06:52.140
she is the pride of
all the people of France!

06:52.220 --> 06:57.140
Especially, since we lost
the war with Prussia in 1871...

06:57.140 --> 07:01.400
The people started to
come to our village in droves.

07:01.570 --> 07:03.230
By the way, see there...

07:03.440 --> 07:06.820
Standing behind you
is Jeanne d'Arc's house.

07:06.820 --> 07:09.360
Ahhh, we are blessed! We are blessed...

07:09.570 --> 07:10.450
Excuse me...

07:10.450 --> 07:12.240
That's not it. What we came for...

07:12.410 --> 07:14.870
We came to search for
Jeanne d'Arc's treasure.

07:15.080 --> 07:16.120
Oh, is that right?

07:16.120 --> 07:19.580
You people have awakened to the
greatness of Jeanne d'Arc, as well?

07:19.580 --> 07:22.000
That is a most admirable attitude.

07:23.190 --> 07:23.900
Excuse me...

07:23.900 --> 07:28.340
In that case, in support of our hopes that France
will prevail once again over the German Empire...

07:28.430 --> 07:29.720
Little boy, there...

07:29.970 --> 07:33.100
you should buy this Jeanne candy.

07:33.220 --> 07:34.640
And the little girl, there...

07:34.640 --> 07:36.100
there's Jeanne cosmetics.

07:36.120 --> 07:37.550
For the kind papa...

07:37.551 --> 07:39.310
there's Jeanne cement instead.

07:40.730 --> 07:41.900
This isn't the place.

07:41.900 --> 07:43.090
It's not even a vegetable stand.

07:42.690 --> 07:44.110
Let's take another look at the map.

07:44.110 --> 07:45.480
It exists!

07:45.480 --> 07:48.030
Jeanne d'Arc's treasure definitely exists!

07:48.400 --> 07:51.820
Jeanne’s childhood friend,
a man named Omette,

07:51.820 --> 07:53.830
had a testimony which still
remains in old literature...

07:53.830 --> 07:59.250
According to that, he said that one day
he saw her bury something in the earth.

07:59.250 --> 08:01.080
In the earth?

08:01.080 --> 08:02.080
Something was...

08:02.420 --> 08:04.250
Hey, old man! Where was this?

08:04.550 --> 08:06.960
The place where Jeanne buried something...

08:06.960 --> 08:08.420
Where was this place?

08:11.430 --> 08:14.350
What a nice old guy!

08:14.470 --> 08:16.430
As a freebie for buying
a pile of cucumbers...

08:16.810 --> 08:19.140
he gives us a treasure map.

08:19.250 --> 08:20.440
We're so lucky!

08:20.440 --> 08:23.610
But, isn't that treasure
map a little suspicious?

08:23.610 --> 08:26.270
Damn! You don't understand anything!

08:27.570 --> 08:30.650
It's a treasure so important
that she buried it in secret...

08:31.240 --> 08:32.950
It has to be pretty big!

08:34.530 --> 08:35.990
Pretty big...

08:36.580 --> 08:38.790
If it's a pretty big treasure...

08:39.000 --> 08:41.660
I might be able to build a very
fast mechanical automobile...

08:42.170 --> 08:45.960
Like, in a cool streamlined design...!

08:45.960 --> 08:46.960
Then...

08:47.090 --> 08:50.050
Kennosuke! You're won-der-ful!

08:51.090 --> 08:52.090
Nice...

08:53.300 --> 08:54.340
Pretty big...

08:55.350 --> 08:57.640
If it's a pretty big treasure...

08:57.850 --> 09:00.640
Maybe I can rebuild it
instead of just doing repairs...

09:00.890 --> 09:03.190
Of course, all the rooms should
have it's own bath and toilet...

09:03.190 --> 09:06.520
And, maybe there could be a
gymnasium and a reception room...!

09:06.520 --> 09:09.610
Thank you, Nadja! Thank you!

09:10.240 --> 09:13.180
'Thank you', they say...

09:13.860 --> 09:17.660
Oh, I didn't do anything.

09:24.040 --> 09:25.040
Oh? Hey!

09:25.080 --> 09:27.630
That must be the place
the old man told us about!

09:28.130 --> 09:31.090
We did it! We did it!
We found the treasure!

09:31.090 --> 09:32.130
Huh? But, this is...

09:32.380 --> 09:33.740
no matter how you look at it...

09:33.840 --> 09:34.840
a church!

09:36.050 --> 09:37.050
A church?!

09:37.530 --> 09:38.580
That is correct.

09:38.740 --> 09:41.200
Jeanne d'Arc is the
pride of the French people.

09:41.200 --> 09:44.200
Or rather, she is the
pride of all Christians.

09:44.460 --> 09:49.300
Even though she was a
most devout Christian...

09:49.300 --> 09:51.840
At the time, she was falsely accused
of being a heretic...

09:51.840 --> 09:56.590
And, as a result, she was burned at
the stake at the age of nineteen...

09:56.680 --> 09:58.760
That was a truly regrettable act.

09:58.760 --> 10:00.580
Um, Excuse me...

09:58.850 --> 10:00.930
However, immediately after her death...

10:00.930 --> 10:04.020
Her sentence was overturned...

10:04.020 --> 10:05.810
And, in more recent times...

10:04.080 --> 10:05.250
Um, Father...

10:05.900 --> 10:09.980
efforts to restore her honour
has become extremely popular.

10:10.400 --> 10:14.700
It seems the Vatican may
canonize her as a saint...

10:14.700 --> 10:17.490
Well, that might not be so impossible.

10:17.700 --> 10:22.160
After all, she is the miraculous Maiden
that was sent to us by God!

10:22.160 --> 10:23.000
And also...

10:23.000 --> 10:26.060
Uhhh! Uh... Umm... We are...

10:28.060 --> 10:29.230
Please, pardon me...

10:29.440 --> 10:32.650
You were here about Jeanne
d'Arc's treasure, weren't you?

10:33.110 --> 10:34.780
Of course, it exists.

10:34.900 --> 10:37.610
Even now, it is sleeping under the earth.

10:37.820 --> 10:38.820
Is that true?

10:38.990 --> 10:42.330
Yes, indeed. It was round...

10:42.660 --> 10:43.830
and it's size was..

10:44.080 --> 10:45.120
about this big.

10:45.330 --> 10:47.670
A-About this big?

10:47.670 --> 10:49.750
Hey, hey... that's pretty specific.

10:50.920 --> 10:52.710
This big!

10:52.710 --> 10:55.420
Do you need a treasure map?

10:56.010 --> 10:56.800
You have one?

10:56.800 --> 10:57.430
Please!

10:57.430 --> 10:58.180
Give it to me!

10:58.180 --> 10:59.840
Of course, I will give it to you...

10:59.850 --> 11:02.560
Yeah! We did it!

11:02.560 --> 11:03.640
However!

11:03.850 --> 11:06.980
For the further
advancement of the church...

11:06.980 --> 11:08.900
please, make a donation.

11:11.860 --> 11:13.956
Here you go. Now you have
nothing to complain about...

11:13.980 --> 11:17.610
Hand over the treasure map.

11:18.490 --> 11:20.450
Hmmm, you go this way...

11:20.570 --> 11:24.240
then cross the bridge, hmm... then...

11:24.240 --> 11:26.580
you go this way, then over here...

11:26.580 --> 11:27.960
Drawn by hand??

11:48.390 --> 11:49.810
Here, eat this.

11:49.980 --> 11:52.520
The cherries this year are excellent!

11:53.650 --> 11:54.820
It's good, isn't it?

11:55.400 --> 11:57.360
Can we really trust this thing?

11:57.610 --> 12:00.046
It feels... like we're just running
errands in the neighborhood?

12:00.070 --> 12:01.110
Hey, Master...

12:01.370 --> 12:04.530
Should we trust a man like this?

12:04.540 --> 12:06.240
It's no use talking to him...

12:06.500 --> 12:08.870
Let's turn back... Master!

12:10.120 --> 12:13.040
You guys don't understand anything, do you

12:13.340 --> 12:14.340
In this world...

12:14.630 --> 12:17.420
There are two kinds of
people who never lie...

12:17.630 --> 12:20.630
They are priests and Native Americans!

12:21.970 --> 12:23.680
Who gave you that map?

12:23.680 --> 12:25.050
A Native American?

12:25.140 --> 12:27.350
A-A priest!

12:27.430 --> 12:29.680
What did the priest say?

12:29.770 --> 12:31.270
Jeanne's treasure...

12:31.270 --> 12:33.310
is even now sleeping under the earth!

12:33.310 --> 12:36.190
Then, this map is really real?

12:36.400 --> 12:39.280
It means that an enormous treasure
is right in front of us!

12:39.530 --> 12:41.860
Ah! W-Wait for us!

12:41.990 --> 12:43.910
Master~!

12:44.580 --> 12:45.580
Treasure...

12:46.370 --> 12:48.370
If it's such an enormous treasure...

12:48.700 --> 12:50.500
I don't have to stop at a
mechanical automobile...

12:50.500 --> 12:52.960
I might be able to build
a mechanical house...

12:53.170 --> 12:56.750
At last, I will be the
king of my own house...

12:56.750 --> 12:57.920
Kennosuke!

12:58.380 --> 13:00.010
Din-n-er!

13:00.510 --> 13:02.180
Okav~~!

13:02.300 --> 13:04.300
Master!!

13:06.050 --> 13:07.050
If it's..

13:07.350 --> 13:09.600
If it's such an enormous treasure...

13:10.390 --> 13:11.890
I don't have to stop at rebuilding...

13:12.140 --> 13:14.650
Maybe I can build an
amusement park in the yard...!

13:14.860 --> 13:17.940
It will be an innovative
and entertaining solution!

13:18.190 --> 13:22.150
Nadja, thank you! Thank you, Nadja!

13:22.910 --> 13:24.990
'Thank you, ' they say...

13:28.870 --> 13:30.080
Your spirits are back up!

13:30.290 --> 13:32.160
That's the way!

13:33.580 --> 13:34.750
And, we're here!

13:35.380 --> 13:36.960
It's 'cause we ran.

13:37.540 --> 13:39.630
What? Jeanne d'Arc?

13:39.800 --> 13:40.800
Yes, sir.

13:41.970 --> 13:43.130
That is correct!

13:43.130 --> 13:46.050
Jeanne d'Arc is the pride
of our Kingdom of France.

13:46.050 --> 13:47.890
Especially in these times,
the people of France...

13:47.890 --> 13:50.810
should gather in support of the king...

13:50.890 --> 13:52.180
and against our mortal enemy, Germany...

13:52.180 --> 13:55.190
in order to recover the
province of Alsace-Lorraine...

13:55.190 --> 13:56.440
Damn it! Stop that!

13:56.650 --> 13:58.690
Jeanne's treasure is not in this house!

13:58.980 --> 14:00.070
What!!

14:00.070 --> 14:01.570
That lying priest...!!!

14:01.650 --> 14:03.070
Damn it! I was fooled!!!

14:03.240 --> 14:05.240
All I have is this treasure map.

14:05.360 --> 14:06.820
What? Really!

14:06.820 --> 14:07.870
A map, again?

14:08.200 --> 14:10.200
But, this one looks real, kind of.

14:11.910 --> 14:14.620
Kind of?! What are you saying?
This map is real!

14:14.920 --> 14:17.250
Then, where's the proof that map is real??

14:17.540 --> 14:18.580
The proof is...

14:18.790 --> 14:20.210
Look at this signature.

14:21.210 --> 14:23.050
This was signed by Omette, himself.

14:23.050 --> 14:25.380
And, according to this writing...

14:25.590 --> 14:28.930
Jeanne's treasure is
related to world peace.

14:29.350 --> 14:30.720
World peace???

14:30.810 --> 14:31.890
If you go, you'll find out!

14:32.350 --> 14:36.350
If you go... Jeanne's super
awesome treasure is waiting there!

14:36.440 --> 14:37.690
Super awesome???

14:37.690 --> 14:38.690
It's super awesome!

14:39.150 --> 14:40.560
Super awesome...

14:40.860 --> 14:43.480
If it's such a super awesome treasure...

14:43.690 --> 14:45.530
I don't have to stop at
a mechanical house...

14:45.530 --> 14:47.820
I might be able to
build a mechanical doll...

14:48.370 --> 14:49.370
That's right...

14:49.530 --> 14:51.870
I'll give that doll a name..

14:51.990 --> 14:54.080
Um... Gakute...

14:54.080 --> 14:55.710
Kennosuke!

14:55.910 --> 14:58.210
You re won-der-ful!

14:58.920 --> 15:00.420
Super awesome...

15:00.840 --> 15:03.090
If it's such a super awesome treasure...

15:03.170 --> 15:04.856
I don't have to stop at
an amusement park...

15:04.880 --> 15:07.130
M-maybe I can build a c-castle...

15:07.720 --> 15:10.890
To live in a castle...
it's every girl's dream...

15:11.100 --> 15:14.720
Girls from r all over the
world will gather at Applefield!

15:14.730 --> 15:18.600
Nadja, thank you! Thank you, Nadja!

15:22.190 --> 15:24.150
I'll take you. come.

15:24.150 --> 15:24.690
Okay!

15:24.780 --> 15:26.530
But, before that...

15:26.650 --> 15:27.900
You, too...

15:28.240 --> 15:29.450
Go, go!

15:29.530 --> 15:31.370
This way!

15:41.380 --> 15:44.130
Look! Jeanne's treasure is past here.

15:44.130 --> 15:46.710
Oh, no! But the path is covered up!

15:49.340 --> 15:51.180
All right! All right!

15:52.010 --> 15:54.430
Look! Jeanne's treasure is past here.

15:54.430 --> 15:57.140
Oh, no! But there's a
rock blocking the path!

16:02.690 --> 16:04.860
Wow! All right! All right!

16:05.150 --> 16:06.860
Who are you people...!?

16:08.700 --> 16:11.200
We're just an ordinary
troupe of traveling performers...

16:12.320 --> 16:15.490
Look! Jeanne's treasure
is at the top of this cliff.

16:15.490 --> 16:18.450
Oh, no! But we can't
climb this steep a slop

16:23.500 --> 16:24.710
Little lady...

16:24.710 --> 16:26.750
You can't fool me...

16:26.760 --> 16:28.010
Huh? What do you mean?

16:28.130 --> 16:30.090
First, there was the boy's fine swordplay.

16:30.090 --> 16:35.350
Next, there was the man's extreme strength.
All that's left is your special talent...

16:35.510 --> 16:38.640
So, show me. Come on, come on, come on.

16:39.890 --> 16:42.850
I'm... but a dancer...

16:45.770 --> 16:46.770
Should I dance?

16:48.610 --> 16:51.990
Look! Jeanne's treasure
is at the top of this cliff.

16:51.990 --> 16:55.200
Oh, no! But even a
dancer can't climb this cliff!

16:55.580 --> 16:56.990
How do we climb it?

16:56.990 --> 16:58.370
Oh, how about an alternate route?

16:58.370 --> 16:59.080
There isn't one.

16:59.080 --> 17:00.290
How about a rope ladder?

17:00.290 --> 17:01.370
Do you want to go back to get it?

17:01.370 --> 17:03.790
Now...

17:03.790 --> 17:04.830
Oh! I remembered!

17:05.670 --> 17:07.090
You remembered something?

17:07.210 --> 17:08.960
It's time for me to feed the pigeons.

17:10.720 --> 17:12.090
Adieu~!

17:12.090 --> 17:13.550
Hey! Wait, damn it!

17:13.720 --> 17:17.390
I paid you a fee for guiding!
Come back and guide!

17:18.060 --> 17:19.060
What do you say?

17:19.060 --> 17:20.720
I did guide you here.

17:21.180 --> 17:24.940
And... if you find it without any
obstacles, it's not very interesting.

17:26.060 --> 17:27.110
That's true...

17:27.110 --> 17:29.020
Um... For a while now...

17:29.150 --> 17:30.940
it's been one obstacle after another.

17:32.150 --> 17:33.200
Adieu ~!

17:33.200 --> 17:34.290
Hey! Wait up! Adieu~!

17:34.291 --> 17:35.680
Ah! Wait!

17:37.080 --> 17:39.120
He's... gone.

17:39.120 --> 17:40.790
How irresponsible can he get?

17:41.460 --> 17:44.210
Well, there is something
to what the old man said...

17:45.000 --> 17:46.330
Anyway, I'm going.

17:47.380 --> 17:48.960
What will the two of you do?

17:49.340 --> 17:51.420
Go or turn back?

17:51.920 --> 17:53.840
Decide for yourselves which way to go.

17:56.010 --> 17:56.840
What do you want to do, Nadja?

17:56.850 --> 17:57.850
What should I do?

18:00.180 --> 18:02.270
I'm going... 'cause I'm a man.

18:02.390 --> 18:03.390
Kennosuke...

18:13.400 --> 18:15.110
But... maybe I won't.

18:24.920 --> 18:27.830
Everybody, keep it
up! It's just a little more!

18:31.340 --> 18:33.090
The treasurer is right in front of us!

18:35.760 --> 18:36.930
The treasure...!

18:37.430 --> 18:39.390
T-The mechanical...

18:40.680 --> 18:43.640
And...

18:44.020 --> 18:44.980
Kennosuke!

18:45.710 --> 18:46.770
Kennosuke~~~!

18:49.110 --> 18:51.270
Just a bit more and
we'll have the treasure!

18:53.530 --> 18:54.940
The treasure...!

18:56.610 --> 18:59.110
For the sake of everyone at Applefield...

19:00.660 --> 19:05.040
I must build castles across the nation...!

19:08.420 --> 19:09.540
Treasure...!

19:09.580 --> 19:11.250
T-Treasure...!

19:11.250 --> 19:12.670
Treasure...!

19:12.750 --> 19:16.880
Hunting~~~!!!

19:16.880 --> 19:24.880
hunting~~~!!!

19:25.390 --> 19:28.020
All right! We'll dig until we find it!

19:28.190 --> 19:30.100
M-Master...!

19:30.400 --> 19:31.400
This is...!

19:38.450 --> 19:41.490
A field... of lilies...

19:46.710 --> 19:49.120
Why? In a ruin like this?

19:49.710 --> 19:52.080
It looks like an old battlefield.

19:58.550 --> 19:59.550
I see.

20:00.590 --> 20:01.680
I understand now.

20:03.100 --> 20:06.390
This is Jeanne d'Arc's treasure.

20:20.740 --> 20:21.740
Jeanne?

20:22.320 --> 20:23.450
Jeanne!

20:24.450 --> 20:25.450
Omette?

20:25.660 --> 20:27.580
Jeanne, what are you doing?

20:28.000 --> 20:30.290
Oh... nothing.

20:37.920 --> 20:41.630
I pray... that this long
war will end soon...

20:42.510 --> 20:45.430
and everyone will live in peace.

20:47.080 --> 20:48.250
I get it.

20:48.620 --> 20:49.960
So that's what this is.

20:50.750 --> 20:52.856
I don't know how much it's
changed as it was passed down...

20:52.880 --> 20:54.340
but, the story that
she buried the bulbs...

20:54.340 --> 20:57.710
turned into treasure with time, huh?

20:57.960 --> 21:01.510
So, does this mean we
were fooled by the villagers?

21:01.880 --> 21:04.260
Damn it!!

21:04.260 --> 21:06.100
But, they didn't lie to us.

21:09.350 --> 21:10.430
Well, guess not...

21:13.580 --> 21:18.800
In all this time, Master has
never actually found any treasure...

21:20.300 --> 21:22.630
Well, they should be back anytime now.

21:22.630 --> 21:25.260
Let's give them a warm welcome.

21:27.390 --> 21:28.560
Oh, well!

21:28.930 --> 21:33.440
After all, there's still plenty of great
treasures that lie asleep all over the world!

21:33.440 --> 21:34.650
Hey, Master?

21:35.440 --> 21:39.690
If you found any treasure,
what are you going to do with it?

21:40.990 --> 21:42.740
Well, it's obvious isn't it?

21:44.110 --> 21:47.490
Use it up until I find the next treasure.

21:49.660 --> 21:51.040
Hey, what are you doing?

21:51.580 --> 21:52.910
Let's hurry up and go home.

21:55.880 --> 21:56.880
Yes, sir!

22:15.370 --> 22:16.995
Paris is sunnier than London

22:16.996 --> 22:18.620
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

22:18.740 --> 22:21.830
- Carmen likes paella more than pasta
- CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

22:22.250 --> 22:25.335
The Queen of Spades is a fickle person

22:25.336 --> 22:28.420
SUPEEDO no jou kimagure yasan

22:29.380 --> 22:30.620
- Indeed
- Kitto

22:33.380 --> 22:35.800
- It's not use worrying about it
- Nayan datte MUDA yo

22:36.380 --> 22:37.945
Que sera sera, sera Sera

22:37.946 --> 22:39.510
KE SERA SERA SERA SERA

22:39.770 --> 22:42.125
Tomorrow's going to
be whatever it was meant

22:42.126 --> 22:44.480
Ashita nante itsumo naru you ni

22:44.560 --> 22:45.940
- To be, to be
- Naru naru

22:46.270 --> 22:48.775
The tree fog won

22:48.776 --> 22:51.280
Sekai KAERU tobi KONKUURU

22:51.740 --> 22:53.700
The world frog-jumping contest

22:53.701 --> 22:55.660
Yuushou shita yo AMAGAERU

22:58.870 --> 23:01.955
Under the kitten's paw

23:01.956 --> 23:05.040
Koneko chan no ashi no ura wa

23:05.460 --> 23:08.545
Is the scent of the sun, right?

23:08.546 --> 23:11.630
Otentou sama no nioi dane

23:14.470 --> 23:16.135
Paris is sunnier than London

23:16.136 --> 23:17.800
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

23:17.890 --> 23:20.890
- Carmen likes paella more than pasta
- CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

23:21.390 --> 23:24.580
It's not the time to hang around

23:24.581 --> 23:27.770
Michikusa shite iru baai ja nai ne

23:28.650 --> 23:30.900
Indeed, indeed

23:30.901 --> 23:33.150
Kitto kitto

23:41.500 --> 23:42.560
- Tomorrow's Nadja
- Tomorrow's Nadja

23:42.690 --> 23:44.480
We have come to..

23:44.480 --> 23:47.240
..an orphanage by a lake in
the Alps, the Le Man Orphanage.

23:47.650 --> 23:51.320
Hey, everyone! Let's do a
tyrolean dance together, shall we?

23:52.010 --> 23:53.010
What?

23:53.200 --> 23:55.120
But, why is Francis here?

23:55.700 --> 23:59.000
What should I do? Will he remember me?

23:59.830 --> 24:02.880
I want to go to him, but my
heart is full of uncertainty.

24:03.920 --> 24:06.760
Tomorrow's Nadja,
Francis in the Morning Light.

24:04.610 --> 24:07.010
Francis In the Morning Light

24:07.010 --> 24:09.050
Now, the Door to Destiny opens!
